SMTP_PORT=587
SMTP_USER=your-email@gmail.com
SMTP_PASS=your-email-app-password
[NEW] 
Backend/database.js
Implement a centralized Database Access Layer.
Check if Supabase keys exist in .env.
If keys are present, initialize @supabase/supabase-js client and query tables.
If keys are missing, fallback to reading and writing locally to data/db.json.
Write automatic migration logic: on start, if connected to Supabase and tables are empty, copy default values from db.json into Supabase.
[MODIFY] 
Backend/package.json
Add dependencies: @supabase/supabase-js, cloudinary, razorpay, multer, nodemailer, dotenv.
[MODIFY] 
Backend/server.js
Initialize dotenv.
Integrate database.js to replace direct fs.readFileSync database access.
Configure cloudinary client.
Configure razorpay client.
Configure nodemailer SMTP transporter.
Expose Authentication OTP Endpoints:
POST /api/auth/send-otp: Generates a 6-digit OTP code, stores it in verification_otps table (with 10-minute expiration), and sends a beautifully styled HTML email to the recipient using Nodemailer.
POST /api/auth/verify-otp: Matches the submitted OTP for the email. If valid, deletes the OTP record and returns a login confirmation/success token.
Expose Cloudinary Media Endpoint:
POST /api/media/upload: Accepts file input, uploads image/video to Cloudinary, and returns { secure_url }.
Expose Razorpay Payment Endpoints:
POST /api/payments/create-order: Generates a Razorpay order ID, writes record to payments table with status created.
POST /api/payments/verify: Verifies Razorpay checkout signature. Updates database payment status to success or failed.
GET /api/payments/transactions: Returns transaction history logs from database for the admin panel.
Frontend Components
[MODIFY] 
Frontend/src/utils/api.ts
Add client helper functions:
sendOtp(email: string): Calls /api/auth/send-otp.
verifyOtp(email: string, otp: string): Calls /api/auth/verify-otp.
uploadMedia(file: File): Sends image/video files via FormData to /api/media/upload.
createPaymentOrder(amount: number, email: string): Calls /api/payments/create-order.
verifyPayment(verificationData: any): Calls /api/payments/verify.
fetchTransactions(): Calls /api/payments/transactions.
[MODIFY] 
Frontend/src/app/(shop)/account/page.tsx
Add dynamic Authentication state (checking if user email is stored in cookie/localStorage).
If not authenticated, display a premium minimal email login form.
Upon entering email, trigger OTP send request and switch form to verification mode.
Verify OTP code. On success, store email and set user session as logged-in.
Update profile tabs to show user's active session email and support secure logouts.
[MODIFY] 
Frontend/src/app/(admin)/admin/products/page.tsx
Integrate a File Upload Input alongside the Image URL text field. Clicking the file input will upload directly to Cloudinary and populate the URL field automatically.
Add "Collection" dropdown (Silent Center, Solitude, Presence, Light, none) to set a product's collection classification.
[MODIFY] 
Frontend/src/app/(admin)/admin/cms/page.tsx
Add File Upload Inputs next to image URLs (Hero Image, Story Banner, Story Anchor Image, Blog Image, Brand Logo) to let the Admin upload assets dynamically.
Add a new "Payments Log" tab to see all Razorpay transactions, amounts, and statuses in a clean table format.
[MODIFY] 
Frontend/src/app/(shop)/collections/silent-center/page.tsx
Adjust filters to match the new dynamic collection classifications, and price range filters.
Verification Plan
Automated Tests
Run npm run build inside Frontend to verify client compile correctness.
Start backend and inspect console output for Supabase initialization and migration tasks.
Manual Verification
Enter an email on the login/account screen, and check inbox for a beautifully formatted VRIX verification email.
Enter the OTP code to log in successfully.
Test uploading an image in the product catalogue and ensure it is uploaded to Cloudinary.
Complete a mockup order checkout to verify Razorpay order generation and database logging.




